@section('content')
  <h1>{{ $title }}</h1>
  <p>The dashboard, at <code>/admin</code>, shows stat cards. A resource adds its cards by implementing the <code>widgets</code> method of the trait.</p>

  <h2>A stat card</h2>
  <p>A card is a <code>StatWidget</code>: a label, such as <code>Tags</code>, and a whole-number value. The dashboard shows the cards of every resource, in the order the resources are passed to the panel builder, and each resource's cards in the order its <code>widgets</code> method returns them.</p>

  <h2>Add a card</h2>
  <p>The <code>Tag</code> resource in <a href="/docs/resources">Resources</a> implements the method. It counts the rows of its table and returns one card.</p>
  <p>The method has this signature: <code>fn widgets(conn: &amp;mut MysqlConnection) -> QueryResult&lt;Vec&lt;StatWidget&gt;&gt;</code>. It runs on a connection from the pool, so it can use any Diesel query. The default returns no cards.</p>
  <p>A derived resource cannot add cards yet. The derive writes the whole trait impl, so a resource that needs cards is written by hand.</p>

  <h2>An empty dashboard</h2>
  <p>When no resource has cards, the dashboard says <code>No stats yet.</code> and tells the developer to implement <code>widgets</code>.</p>

  <h2>Not built yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>A table of the latest records.</strong> The dashboard shows stat cards only.</li>
    <li><strong>Charts.</strong> Charts are out of scope for v1.</li>
    <li><strong>Links and ordering.</strong> A card does not link anywhere, and the order is fixed by the resources' order.</li>
  </ul>
@endsection
